---
// How X-Forwarded-For grows hop by hop, and which entry a rate limiter should key on.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 520" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="rl-xff-t rl-xff-d">
  <title id="rl-xff-t">Reading the client address behind two proxies</title>
  <desc id="rl-xff-d">
    A client at 203.0.113.7 sends a request that already carries a forged X-Forwarded-For of
    6.6.6.6. The CDN at 198.51.100.2 appends the address it saw, 203.0.113.7. The load balancer at
    10.0.0.5 appends the address it saw, the CDN's. The app sees a connection from 10.0.0.5 and the
    header "6.6.6.6, 203.0.113.7, 198.51.100.2". Reading from the right and skipping your own
    proxies, the first address that is not yours, 203.0.113.7, is the real client. The leftmost
    entry was typed by the client and must be ignored.
  </desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="rl-xff-flow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" style="fill: var(--viz-flow)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <g font-size="19" text-anchor="middle">
    <rect x="8" y="16" width="176" height="60" rx="14" style="fill: var(--viz-client-soft); stroke: var(--viz-client)" stroke-width="2" />
    <text x="96" y="42" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Client</text>
    <text x="96" y="66" style="fill: var(--viz-muted); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">203.0.113.7</text>

    <rect x="8" y="116" width="176" height="60" rx="6" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" stroke-width="2" />
    <text x="96" y="142" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">CDN</text>
    <text x="96" y="166" style="fill: var(--viz-muted); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">198.51.100.2</text>

    <rect x="8" y="216" width="176" height="60" rx="6" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" stroke-width="2" />
    <text x="96" y="242" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Load balancer</text>
    <text x="96" y="266" style="fill: var(--viz-muted); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">10.0.0.5</text>

    <rect x="8" y="316" width="176" height="48" rx="6" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" stroke-width="2" />
    <text x="96" y="347" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">App</text>
  </g>

  <g stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-flow)" marker-end="url(#rl-xff-flow)">
    <line x1="96" y1="78" x2="96" y2="112" />
    <line x1="96" y1="178" x2="96" y2="212" />
    <line x1="96" y1="278" x2="96" y2="312" />
  </g>

  <!-- What each hop does to the header. -->
  <g font-size="19">
    <text x="200" y="42" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">forges XFF:</text>
    <text x="200" y="66" style="fill: var(--viz-bad); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">6.6.6.6</text>
    <text x="200" y="142" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">appends:</text>
    <text x="200" y="166" style="fill: var(--viz-ok); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">203.0.113.7</text>
    <text x="200" y="242" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">appends:</text>
    <text x="200" y="266" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">198.51.100.2</text>
    <text x="200" y="347" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">peer: <tspan style="font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">10.0.0.5</tspan></text>
  </g>

  <line x1="8" y1="388" x2="392" y2="388" stroke-width="1" style="stroke: var(--viz-stroke)" />
  <text x="8" y="418" font-size="19" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Read from the right:</text>
  <g font-size="19">
    <text x="8" y="452" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">198.51.100.2</text>
    <text x="392" y="452" text-anchor="end" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">our CDN, skip</text>
    <text x="8" y="482" style="fill: var(--viz-ok); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">203.0.113.7</text>
    <text x="392" y="482" text-anchor="end" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ok)">the key</text>
    <text x="8" y="512" style="fill: var(--viz-bad); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">6.6.6.6</text>
    <text x="392" y="512" text-anchor="end" style="fill: var(--viz-bad)">forged, ignore</text>
  </g>
</svg>
